Source: the pre-merge integration smoke for kai-cli#118, 2026-09-17:
`kai review-commit --fast --format json` on the kai-desktop #429 change
(scratch repo e2e-429 @ c478d2f), KAI_REVIEW_MODEL=z-ai/glm-5.2, all traffic
captured through a logging proxy. Draft anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5, challenger
z-ai/glm-5.2 (both confirmed from response metadata).

Fields: draft (what was challenged), issues (as handed to the challenger),
sources (what the challenger received, line-number prefixes stripped, including
its one review_shell result), submitted (the raw submit_review arguments, byte
for byte), mainError (what main did with it).

Why this specimen: its one per-allegation judgment was valid (refuted, two
resolving location citations), but its rewritten review opened with the
REVIEW-DATA marker and carried no coda fields, so main rejected the rewrite and
withheld the whole review. The production failure of the same class on
kai-desktop#429 (run 89bdabb8: "revised review added an unchecked or rejected
allegation") logged only its error line — its payload was never captured — and
eight captured attempts with main's binary on the same change did not reproduce
that exact error (7 self-consistent reviews, 1 malformed-JSON failure).
